<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Mihon's splash theme points at @drawable/ic_mihon_splash. Redefining that name here swaps the
  launch icon for ours; the theme itself is Mihon's and stays untouched.

  The name is theirs, which is why this file is worth a comment: it is an override, not a new
  resource, and it disappears the moment we own the splash theme.

  It points at the unframed lockup rather than the launcher foreground, and the difference is the
  whole fix. The launcher artwork carries the brand's panel frame — a dark rectangle edged in white
  sketch lines — which works on a launcher because a paper-coloured background layer sits behind it.
  A splash has no background layer, so on ink black that frame's interior merges with the screen and
  the frame itself reads as a grey slab floating in the void.

  Built by docs/branding/build-wordmark.py, and a single file now rather than three. The mark used
  to be blue letters over a Japanese line, and that line had to be recoloured between the light and
  dark configurations or it vanished into whichever background it was not drawn for. It is now the
  white brush letters alone, and @color/splash is ink black in *both* configurations — so there is
  nothing left to vary, and drawable-nodpi answers every case.
-->
<bitmap xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:gravity="fill"
    android:src="@drawable/animato_splash_mark" />
